WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.224
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:03.274 --> 00:00:05.898
Tiny Coders, video 2.

3
00:00:05.948 --> 00:00:07.680
Order matters.

4
00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:12.571
If the steps are in the wrong order, the result is wrong

5
00:00:12.621 --> 00:00:15.400
— even when every step is good on its own.

6
00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.103
Think about brushing teeth.

7
00:00:19.153 --> 00:00:23.730
Wet the brush, put toothpaste on, brush, then rinse.

8
00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:28.090
Swap the first and last steps and the plan fails.

9
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:31.958
The same idea shows up in code.

10
00:00:32.008 --> 00:00:36.908
A robot that drives before the motors are on will sit still.

11
00:00:36.958 --> 00:00:39.630
Order is part of the instruction.

12
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.361
Let us recap.

13
00:00:42.411 --> 00:00:45.285
A sequence is steps in order.

14
00:00:45.335 --> 00:00:48.815
Wrong order means the wrong result.

15
00:00:48.865 --> 00:00:51.840
Next: Patterns you can repeat.
